{
  "Name": "Okta - User Aggregates",
  "Description": "Every hour, rebuilds the Okta user-directory aggregates and saves them to the resource okta_user_aggregates (columns ts,metric,key,value,rowkey). @users takes the newest record per user from the last 25 hours of $OKTA_USERS (which always includes the hosted ingester's daily full user snapshot); one inner query per metric counts them (status, user type, division, department, job title, manager, timezone, credential provider type and name, last sign-in and password age of active users, average password age, average days from created to activated); the main query stacks the results with dump -p and writes them with table -save -update rowkey.\n\nrowkey is metric|key for snapshot rows and ts|metric|key for the last_signin_history and password_age_history rows. -update replaces resource rows whose rowkey is in the new results and keeps every other row, so the history grows by one point per run and is never pruned, and a snapshot key that no longer occurs (a department nobody is in any more, a status or bucket that dropped to zero) keeps its last count. A run that finds no users changes nothing.\n\nThe Okta User Overview and User Authentication Overview dashboards and the timezone table on Okta Sign-In Locations read only that resource (dump -r); detections never read it. Needs the hosted ingester's daily full user snapshot to cover users who have not changed, and its owner needs permission to write resources.",
  "Labels": [
    "okta",
    "aggregates",
    "agg"
  ],
  "Schedule": "17 * * * *",
  "Duration": -90000,
  "DefaultDeploymentRules": {
    "Disabled": false,
    "RunImmediately": true
  },
  "ScheduledType": "search",
  "GUID": "9b1ce589-ac0f-5261-9e71-1e11e54a8e4c",
